   ],
   "definition_quote": "Let $\\xX \\subset \\RR^d$ be a compact set of actions and $\\theta \\in \\RR^d$ be an unknown parameter. For each action $x\\in \\xX$, let $A_x \\in \\RR^{d \\times m}$ be a known linear observation operator. ... receives an $m$-dimensional observation $\\a_t = A_{x_t}^\\T\\theta + \\epsilon_t$ ... The reward for the learner is $\\ip{x_t,\\theta}$ and is not observed. A game is called globally observable if x - y \\in span(A_z : z \\in X) for all x, y."
  },
